@startuml Makicol_ER_v6
!theme plain
title Makicol Marketplace — Data model (v6 — esquema "makicol", prefijo Mk, coexistencia aislada con Feria Artesanal)
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

note as coexistencia
  COEXISTENCIA CON FERIA ARTESANAL (misma BD Azure SQL, mismo App Service)
  - Feria Artesanal vive en el esquema "dbo" (Regiones, Departamentos, Municipios,
    Artesanos, Ediciones, Dias, Eventos, Fotos, Usuarios, RefreshTokens, AuditLogs...).
    NO se toca ninguna de sus tablas, migraciones ni código.
  - Makicol vive COMPLETO en el esquema "makicol" y todas sus tablas llevan
    el prefijo "Mk". Tiene su propio DbContext, su propia tabla de historial
    de migraciones (makicol.__EFMigrationsHistory) y su propia autenticación.
  - REGLA: cero foreign keys, vistas o consultas cruzadas entre "dbo" y "makicol".
    Lo único compartido es la cadena de conexión y el host (para evitar costos
    duplicados hasta que Makicol se separe a sus propios recursos).
  - Salida futura: "dotnet ef migrations script --context MakicolDbContext"
    reproduce el esquema "makicol" íntegro en una BD nueva sin renombrar nada.
end note

package "Esquema: makicol" {

entity "MkUser" as user {
  * id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  name : text
  email : text <<unique>>
  password_hash : text
  role : enum(buyer, artisan, support, auditor)
  registration_date : date
  language : text <<es, en, de, ...>>
  ..audit..
  created_at : datetimeoffset
  updated_at : datetimeoffset
  updated_by : UUID <<FK -> MkUser.id>>
}

entity "MkRefreshToken" as refresh_token {
  * id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  user_id : UUID <<FK>>
  token : text
  expires_at : datetimeoffset
  is_revoked : boolean
  created_at : datetimeoffset
}
note right of refresh_token
  Autenticación PROPIA de Makicol (JWT + refresh).
  No reutiliza dbo.Usuarios ni dbo.RefreshTokens
  de Feria: solo comparte el mecanismo/librería.
end note

entity "MkBuyerProfile" as buyer_profile {
  * user_id : UUID <<PK, FK>>
  --
  city : text
  shipping_address : text
  timezone : text <<IANA, e.g. America/New_York>>
}

entity "MkArtisanProfile" as artisan_profile {
  * user_id : UUID <<PK, FK>>
  --
  region : text
  city : text
  craft_type : text
  bio : text
  start_year : int
  materials : text[]
  payment_method : enum(nequi, daviplata, pse)
  timezone : text <<IANA, e.g. Europe/Madrid>>
  verification_status_id : int <<FK>>
  ..audit..
  created_at : datetimeoffset
  updated_at : datetimeoffset
  updated_by : UUID <<FK -> MkUser.id>>
}
note right of artisan_profile
  region / city son texto propio de Makicol.
  NO referencian dbo.Municipios de Feria
  (regla de cero cruces entre esquemas).
end note

entity "MkSupportAgent" as support_agent {
  * user_id : UUID <<PK, FK>>
  --
  level : text
}

entity "MkProduct" as product {
  * id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  artisan_id : UUID <<FK>>
  name : text
  category : text
  region : text
  price : numeric
  description : text
  image_url : text
  sold_count : int
  is_active : boolean <<default true>>
  ..audit..
  created_at : datetimeoffset
  created_by : UUID <<FK -> MkUser.id>>
  updated_at : datetimeoffset
  updated_by : UUID <<FK -> MkUser.id>>
}
note right of product
  "is_active" es un booleano simple, NO una tabla
  de estados: interruptor de 2 valores libremente
  reversible, sin secuencia que proteger. Excepción
  intencional al patrón MkXStatus / MkXStatusTransition.
end note

entity "MkOrder" as order {
  * id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  buyer_id : UUID <<FK>>
  placed_at : datetimeoffset
  total : numeric
  status_id : int <<FK>>
  origin_timezone : text <<IANA, copy from buyer profile>>
  ..audit..
  created_at : datetimeoffset
  updated_at : datetimeoffset
  updated_by : UUID <<FK -> MkUser.id>>
}

entity "MkOrderStatus" as order_status {
  * id : int <<PK>>
  --
  name : text <<seed: Recibido, En preparación, Enviado, Entregado>>
  display_order : int
  is_terminal : boolean
}

entity "MkOrderStatusTransition" as order_status_transition {
  * from_status_id : int <<PK, FK>>
  * to_status_id : int <<PK, FK>>
  --
  allowed_role : enum(buyer, artisan, system)
}
note right of order_status_transition
  Por ahora solo dato de referencia (documenta
  saltos válidos), sin trigger. Se expande a
  validación real en una fase futura.
end note

entity "MkOrderItem" as order_item {
  * id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  order_id : UUID <<FK>>
  product_id : UUID <<FK>>
  quantity : int
  unit_price : numeric
}

entity "MkReview" as review {
  * id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  author_id : UUID <<FK>>
  product_id : UUID <<FK>>
  rating : int
  comment : text
  posted_on : date
}

entity "MkWishlistItem" as wishlist_item {
  * buyer_id : UUID <<PK, FK>>
  * product_id : UUID <<PK, FK>>
  --
  added_on : date
}

entity "MkSupportCase" as support_case {
  * id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  requester_id : UUID <<FK>>
  requester_role : enum(buyer, artisan)
  category : text
  subject : text
  status_id : int <<FK>>
  priority : enum(low, medium, high)
  related_order_id : UUID <<FK, nullable>>
  ..audit..
  created_at : datetimeoffset
  updated_at : datetimeoffset
  updated_by : UUID <<FK -> MkUser.id, agent or requester>>
}

entity "MkSupportCaseStatus" as support_case_status {
  * id : int <<PK>>
  --
  name : text <<seed: Abierto, En proceso, Resuelto, Cerrado>>
  display_order : int
  is_terminal : boolean
}

entity "MkSupportCaseStatusTransition" as support_case_status_transition {
  * from_status_id : int <<PK, FK>>
  * to_status_id : int <<PK, FK>>
  --
  allowed_role : enum(support, system)
}
note right of support_case_status_transition
  Dato de referencia por ahora (incluye
  "Cerrado -> Abierto" para reapertura).
end note

entity "MkSupportMessage" as support_message {
  * id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  case_id : UUID <<FK>>
  author_id : UUID <<FK>>
  author_role : enum(buyer, artisan, support)
  body : text
  sent_at : datetimeoffset
}

entity "MkFaqItem" as faq_item {
  * id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  question : text
  answer : text
  category : text
  target_role : enum(buyer, artisan)
}

entity "MkArtisanVerificationStatus" as artisan_verification_status {
  * id : int <<PK>>
  --
  name : text <<seed: Pendiente, Verificado, Rechazado>>
  display_order : int
  is_terminal : boolean
}

entity "MkArtisanVerificationStatusTransition" as artisan_verification_status_transition {
  * from_status_id : int <<PK, FK>>
  * to_status_id : int <<PK, FK>>
  --
  allowed_role : enum(system, support)
}
note right of artisan_verification_status_transition
  Dato de referencia por ahora. Verificación hoy
  automática (24h post-registro); deja espacio
  para revisión manual futura.
end note

entity "MkInternationalShipment" as international_shipment {
  * id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  order_id : UUID <<FK, unique>>
  status_id : int <<FK>>
  courier : text <<DHL, FedEx, etc.>>
  tracking_number : text
  certificate_of_origin_ref : text
  ..audit..
  created_at : datetimeoffset
  updated_at : datetimeoffset
  updated_by : UUID <<FK -> MkUser.id>>
}
note right of international_shipment
  Seguimiento granular específico del piloto
  internacional (ver /envios-internacionales).
  Pedidos nacionales NO generan esta entidad.
  1 MkOrder internacional <-> 1 MkInternationalShipment.
end note

entity "MkInternationalShipmentStatus" as international_shipment_status {
  * id : int <<PK>>
  --
  name : text <<seed: Preparación, Trámites de exportación, En tránsito, Aduana EE.UU., Entregado>>
  display_order : int
  is_terminal : boolean
}

entity "MkInternationalShipmentStatusTransition" as international_shipment_status_transition {
  * from_status_id : int <<PK, FK>>
  * to_status_id : int <<PK, FK>>
  --
  allowed_role : enum(artisan, support, system)
}

entity "MkMonthlyMetric" as monthly_metric {
  * month : date <<PK>>
  --
  gmv : numeric
  completed_orders : int
  total_cases : int
}
note right of monthly_metric
  Vista/agregado para el rol Auditor,
  calculada sobre MkOrder y MkSupportCase.
  No es tabla transaccional.
end note

entity "MkActivityLog" as activity_log {
  * id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  entity_type : enum(user, artisan_profile, product, order, support_case, international_shipment, ...)
  entity_id : UUID
  action : enum(create, update, delete)
  user_id : UUID <<FK -> MkUser.id>>
  occurred_at : datetimeoffset
  changes : jsonb <<diff before/after, includes status changes>>
}
note right of activity_log
  Log de auditoría append-only de Makicol,
  independiente de dbo.AuditLogs de Feria.
  Registra cada creación/modificación/eliminación
  y cada transición de estado. entity_type +
  entity_id es referencia polimórfica (sin FK física).
end note

note bottom of order
  ESTRATEGIA DE TIEMPOS (multi-región):
  - Instantes reales -> datetimeoffset (Azure SQL):
    instante UTC canónico + offset original del usuario.
  - "date" solo para calendario sin hora:
    MkUser.registration_date, MkReview.posted_on,
    MkWishlistItem.added_on, MkMonthlyMetric.month.
  - MkBuyerProfile / MkArtisanProfile guardan timezone (IANA).
  - El frontend Angular recibe ISO 8601 y formatea con
    Intl.DateTimeFormat (TimezoneService + pipe mktDate).
end note

}

user ||--o{ refresh_token : "posee"
user ||--o| buyer_profile
user ||--o| artisan_profile
user ||--o| support_agent

artisan_verification_status ||--o{ artisan_profile : "estado actual"
artisan_verification_status_transition }o--|| artisan_verification_status : from/to

artisan_profile ||--o{ product : publica

user ||--o{ order : compra
order_status ||--o{ order : "estado actual"
order_status_transition }o--|| order_status : from/to
order ||--|{ order_item : contiene
product ||--o{ order_item : "vendido en"
order ||--o| international_shipment : "genera (si es internacional)"
international_shipment_status ||--o{ international_shipment : "estado actual"
international_shipment_status_transition }o--|| international_shipment_status : from/to

user ||--o{ review : escribe
product ||--o{ review : recibe

user ||--o{ wishlist_item : guarda
product ||--o{ wishlist_item : "es guardado en"

user ||--o{ support_case : "abre (como solicitante)"
support_case_status ||--o{ support_case : "estado actual"
support_case_status_transition }o--|| support_case_status : from/to
support_case ||--o{ support_message : contiene
user ||--o{ support_message : "escribe (autor)"
support_case }o--o| order : "referencia (opcional)"

user ||--o{ activity_log : "genera (autor del cambio)"

@enduml
